{"r":"jwf","lane":{"p":487,"e":[{"h":"جَوَفٌ","t":["The ",[1,"being"]," [",[1,"hollow,"]," or] ",[1,"wide and hollow within:"]," (PS:) or the ",[1,"being empty, vacant,"]," or ",[1,"void:"]," an inf. n. of which the verb is of the class of ",[2,"تَعِبَ"]," [i. e. ",[2,"جَافَ"],", originally ",[2,"جَوِفَ"],", like ",[2,"خَافَ"],", sec. pers. ",[2,"جِفْتَ"],", aor. ",[2,"يَجَافُ"],"]: (Msb:) the ",[1,"being wide, spacious,"]," or ",[1,"ample:"]," (K:) the inf. n., or source, whence ",[2,"شَىْءٌ أَجْوَفُ"],". (S.) [See also 10.] -A2- ",[2,"جَافَهُ"],", [aor. ",[2,"يَجُوفُ"],",] inf. n. ",[2,"جَوْفٌ"],", ",[1,"It reached his"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"inside,"]," or ",[1,"interior,"]," &c.]. (TA.) ",[1,"It"]," (medicine) ",[1,"entered his"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (TA. [See also 8.]) And ",[2,"جَافَتْهُ الجِرَاحَةُ"],[1,"The wound reached his"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (Msb.) ― -b2- ",[2,"طَعَنَهُ فَجَافَهُ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"اجافهُ"],", ",[1,"He pierced him and pierced his"],[2,"جَوْف"],": (Mgh, Msb:) and ↓ ",[2,"جوّفهُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"تَجْوِيفٌ"],", ",[1,"he pierced him in his"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (TA.) ",[2,"جُفْتُهُ بِالطَّعْنَةِ"],", and ",[2,"الطَّعْنَةَ"]," ↓ ",[2,"أَجَفْتُهُ"],", ",[1,"I made the spear-wound,"]," or ",[1,"the like, to reach his"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (Ks, A 'Obeyd, S, K.) ",[2,"جَافَ الصَّيْدَ"],[1,"He made the arrow to enter the"],[2,"جَوْف"],[1,"of the object of the chase."]," (TA.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"تَجْوِيفٌ","t":["The ",[1,"making"]," [a thing] ",[1,"hollow,"]," or ",[1,"empty in the middle."]," (KL, PS.) You say, ",[2,"جوّفهُ"],", inf. n. ",[2,"تَجْوِيفٌ"],", [",[1,"He made it hollow; hollowed it out;"],"] ",[1,"he made it to have a"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (Msb.) And of a thing that is ",[2,"مُجَوَّف"],", (S, K,) i. e. ",[2,"أجْوَف"],", (S,) you say, ",[2,"فِيهِ تَجْوِيفٌ"]," [",[1,"In it is a hollowing out;"]," meaning ",[1,"a hollow,"]," in which sense ",[2,"تجويف"]," has a pl., namely, ",[2,"تَجَاوِيفُ"],"]. (S, K.) ― -b2- See also 1."],"f":"2"},{"h":"أَجْوَفَ","t":["see 1, in two places. ― -b2- ",[2,"اجاف البَابَ"]," (tropical:) ",[1,"He shut,"]," or ",[1,"closed, the door."]," (S, K, TA.) Hence, in a trad., ",[2,"وَأَجِيفُوا الأَبْوَاَ وَأَطْفِئُوا المَصَابِيحَ"]," [",[1,"And shut ye the doors, and extinguish the lamps"],"]. (TA.)"],"f":"4"},{"h":"تجوّف","t":[[1,"It was,"]," or ",[1,"became, hollow,"]," or ",[1,"empty within."]," (KL.) -A2- ",[2,"تجوّفهُ"],": see 8. ― -b2- ",[2,"تَجَوَّفَتِ الخُوصَةُ"],[2,"العَرْفَجَ"],[1,"The leaf was in the"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"inside"],"] ",[1,"of the"]," [",[1,"plant called"],"] ",[2,"عرفج"],", ",[1,"not having yet come forth."]," (S.)"],"f":"5"},{"h":"اجتافهُ","t":[[1,"He entered its"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"inside,"]," or ",[1,"interior; he entered into the midst of it"],"]; as also ↓ ",[2,"تجوّفهُ"],". (S, K.) [See an ex. in a verse of Lebeed, voce ",[2,"أَصْلٌ"],": and see also 1.]"],"f":"8"},{"h":"استجاف","t":[[1,"It"]," (a thing) ",[1,"became wide, spacious,"]," or ",[1,"ample."]," (S, K.) [See also 1, first sentence.] -A2- ",[2,"استجافهُ"],[1,"He found it"]," (a place) to be ",[2,"أَجْوَف"]," [i. e. ",[1,"hollow,"]," or ",[1,"empty within;"]," or ",[1,"wide, spacious,"]," or ",[1,"ample"],"]. (O, L, K.)"],"f":"10"},{"h":"جَوْفٌ","t":["[",[1,"A hollow; an interior empty, vacant,"]," or ",[1,"void, space;"],"] ",[1,"a vacancy:"]," pl. ",[2,"أَجْوَافٌ"],": this is the primary signification: then it was used in relation to a thing capable of being occupied and of being unoccupied; so as to be applied in the sense next following. (Msb.) ― -b2- The ",[1,"inside,"]," or ",[1,"interior,"]," (Msb, KL,) of a house [&c.]. (Msb.) ― -b3- [The ",[1,"midst,"]," or ",[1,"middle,"]," of a thing.] ― -b4- ",[1,"A low,"]," or ",[1,"depressed,"]," (S, K, TA,) ",[1,"and wide,"]," (TA,) ",[1,"tract,"]," or ",[1,"portion, of land,"]," or ",[1,"ground:"]," (S, K, TA:) ",[1,"what is wider than the"],[2,"شِعْب"],"; ",[1,"the"]," [",[1,"water-courses termed"],"] ",[2,"تِلَاع"],", ",[1,"and the valleys, flow into it; and it has"],[2,"جِرَفَة"]," [or ",[1,"abrupt, water-worn, banks"],"]: ",[1,"sometimes it is wider than a valley, and deeper:"]," and ",[1,"sometimes it is a plain,"]," or ",[1,"soft, tract, that retains water:"]," and ",[1,"sometimes it is completely round, so that it retains water:"]," accord. to IAar, it signifies ",[1,"a valley:"]," or, as some say, the ",[1,"interior"]," (",[2,"بَطْن"],") ",[1,"of a valley."]," (TA.) ― -b5- The ",[1,"belly,"]," or ",[1,"abdomen,"]," of a man: (S, K:) or, accord. to ISd, the ",[1,"interior of the belly:"]," and the ",[1,"part upon which close the shoulder-blades and the upper arms and the ribs and the two flanks"]," (",[2,"الصُّقْلَانِ"],"): (TA:) the ",[1,"chest,"]," or ",[1,"thorax;"]," i. e., the ",[1,"part of the body that is separated from the"],[2,"بَطْن"]," [or ",[1,"belly,"]," or ",[1,"abdomen,"],"] ",[1,"by the"],[2,"حِجَاب"]," [or ",[1,"diaphragm,"]," or ",[1,"midriff"],"]; ",[1,"containing the heart and its appertenances:"]," (Zj in his “ Khalk el-Insán: ”) pl. as above. (TA.) See also ",[2,"جَائِفٌ"],". It is one of the words that are not used adverbially except with prepositions. (Sb, TA.) It is said in a trad., ",[2,"لَا تَنْسَوُا الجَوْفَ"],[2,"وَمَا وَعَى"]," [",[1,"Forget not ye the"],[2,"جوف"],[1,"and what it hath collected"],"]; meaning what enters into it, of food and beverage: but some say that ",[2,"الجوف"]," here means ",[1,"the belly and the"],[2,"فَرْج"]," [or ",[1,"vulva,"]," or ",[1,"pudendum muliebre"],"], together, which are also called ↓ ",[2,"الأَجْوَفَانِ"],": and some say that the meaning is, ",[1,"the heart and what it hath retained, and kept in memory,"]," of the knowledge of God. (A 'Obeyd, TA.) ― -b6- ",[2,"الأَجْوَافُ"]," is also applied by the people of El-Ghowr (K) and of El-Yemen (TA) to ",[1,"The tents"]," (",[2,"فَسَاطِيط"],") ",[1,"of their"],[2,"عُمَّال"]," [or ",[1,"governors,"]," or ",[1,"collectors of the poor-rates"],"]. (K.) ― -b7- ",[2,"جَوْفُ اللَّيْلِ"],[2,"الآخِرُ"],", occurring in a trad., means (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The last third of the night:"]," [or] ",[1,"the fifth of the sixths of the night:"]," (K:) not the half, as some assert. (TA.)"]},{"h":"جَوْفِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],"."]},{"h":"جُوفِىٌّ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],". -A2- Also, and without tesh-deed, (S, K,) [app. meaning, when with the article ",[2,"ال"],", written and pronounced ",[2,"الجُوفِى"],",] in the accus. case ",[2,"جُوفِيًا"],", by poetic license, (S,) ",[1,"A species of fish;"]," and so ↓ ",[2,"جُوَافٌ"],". (S, K.)"]},{"h":"جُوفَانٌ","t":["The ",[1,"penis of an ass:"]," (El-Muärrij, K:) and ",[1,"of a man."]," (TA.)"]},{"h":"جُوَافٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"جُوفِىٌّ"],"."]},{"h":"جَائِفٌ","t":[[1,"Reaching the"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (Msb.) [Hence,] ",[2,"طَعْنَةٌ جَائِفَةٌ"],", (S, Mgh, K, &c.,) or ",[2,"جِرَاحَةٌ جَائِفَةٌ"],", (Msb,) ",[1,"A spear-wound,"]," or ",[1,"the like, that reaches the"]," ↓ ",[2,"جَوْف"],", (S, Mgh, Msb, K,) by which is here meant [the ",[1,"interior of the body"]," or ",[1,"head,"]," or], accord. to IAth, ",[1,"any vital part,"]," as ",[1,"the belly"]," and ",[1,"the brain:"]," (TA:) and sometimes, ",[1,"that penetrates into the"],[2,"جوف"],": (A 'Obeyd, S, Mgh:) and ",[1,"that passes through"]," also: (A 'Obeyd, S:) and said to be ",[1,"such as is in the pit between the collarbones,"]," and ",[1,"in the pubes;"]," but not in the neck, nor in the throat, nor in the thigh, nor in the leg: (Mgh:) not if it reaches the interior of the bone of the thigh: (Msb:) opposed to ",[2,"جَالِفَةٌ"],". (S in art. ",[2,"جلف"],".) ― -b2- Hence, ",[2,"جَائِفَةٌ"]," is applied to (tropical:) ",[1,"A great fault"]," or ",[1,"imperfection"]," or ",[1,"vice."]," (TA from a trad.) ― -b3- ",[2,"تَلْعَةٌ جَائِفَةٌ"],[1,"A deep"]," [",[1,"water-course,"]," &c.: see ",[2,"تلعه"],"]: pl. ",[2,"جَوَائِفُ"],". (K, TA. [In the CK, ",[2,"قَصِيرَةٌ"]," is erroneously put for ",[2,"قَعِيرَةٌ"],".]) ― -b4- ",[2,"جَوَائِفُ النَّفْسِ"],[1,"The deep recesses of the"],[2,"جَوْفَ"]," [or ",[1,"chest"],"] ",[1,"in the places where the soul has its seat;"]," expl. by ",[2,"مَا تَقَعَّرَ مِنَ الجَوْفِ فِى مَقَارِّ الرُّوحِ"],". (L, K.) So in the phrase, used by El-Farezdak, ",[2,"وَرَدَّ النَّفْسَ بَيْنَ الجَوَائِفِ"]," [",[1,"And he drove back the soul into the midst of the deep recesses of the chest"],"]: (L, TA:) but some read ",[2,"بين الشَّرَاسِفِ"],". (TA.) ― -b5- ",[2,"الجَائِفُ"]," [",[1,"The cephalic vein;"],"] ",[1,"a vein that runs along the upper arm to the"]," [",[1,"cartilage called"],"] ",[2,"نَغْض"],[1,"of the shoulder-blade;"]," it is ",[1,"the"],[2,"فَلِيق"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"أَجْوَفُ","t":[[1,"Having a"],[2,"جَوْف"],"; (TA;) [i. e.,] ",[1,"hollow,"]," or ",[1,"empty within;"]," (KL, PS;) ",[1,"having in it a"],[2,"تَجْوِيف"]," [or ",[1,"hollowing out,"]," meaning ",[1,"a hollow"],"], (S,) and so ↓ ",[2,"مُجَوَّفٌ"],": (S, K: [but the latter is more properly rendered ",[1,"hollowed,"]," or ",[1,"hollowed out:"],"]) ",[1,"empty, vacant,"]," or ",[1,"void:"]," (Msb:) ",[1,"wide, spacious,"]," or ",[1,"ample;"]," (S, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"مُسْتَجَافٌ"],", (S, TA,) and ↓ ",[2,"جُوفِىٌّ"],", with damm, (K,) thus correctly written, being a rel. n. altered from the original form, like ",[2,"سُهْلِىٌّ"]," and ",[2,"دُهْرِىٌّ"],", (Sgh, TA,) but meaning ",[1,"wide in the"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"belly,"]," &c.], written by J [in the S] ↓ ",[2,"جَوْفِىٌّ"],", with fet-h: (TA:) ",[1,"great in the"],[2,"جَوْف"],"; (TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"مَجُوفٌ"],"; (AO, S, K;) each applied to a man: (TA:) [fem. ",[2,"جَوْفَآءُ"],":] pl. ",[2,"جُوفٌ"],". (TA.) You say ",[2,"لُؤْلُؤٌ أَجْوَفُ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"مُجَوَّفٌ"],", [",[1,"Hollow,"]," and ",[1,"hollowed, pearls;"]," or] both signify the same. (TA.) And ",[2,"قَنَاةٌ جَوْفَآءُ"],[1,"An empty"]," [or ",[1,"a hollow"],"] ",[1,"cane,"]," or ",[1,"reed:"]," (K:) and in like manner, ",[2,"شَجَرَةٌ"]," [",[1,"a tree"],"]; (S, K;) ",[1,"having a"],[2,"جَوْف"],". (S.) And ",[2,"دَلْوٌ جَوْفَآءُ"],[1,"A wide,"]," or ",[1,"an ample, bucket:"]," (K:) and ",[2,"دِلَآءٌ جَوفٌ"],[1,"wide,"]," or ",[1,"ample, buckets:"]," (S:) and ",[2,"قِدْرٌ جَوْفَآءُ"],[1,"a wide, capacious, cooking-pot."]," (Ham p. 719.) And ",[2,"الأَجْوَفُ"],[1,"The lion that is great in the"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"belly,"]," &c.]. (K.) And ",[2,"الأَجْوَفَانِ"],[1,"The belly and the"],[2,"فَرْج"]," [or ",[1,"vulva,"]," or ",[1,"pudendum muliebre"],"]; (S, K;) because of their width. (TA.) See also ",[2,"جَوْفٌ"],". Hence the trad., ",[2,"إِنَّ أَخْوَفَ مَا أَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمُ الأَجْوَفَانِ"]," [",[1,"Verily what I most fear for you are the belly and the vulva"],"]. (TA.) ― -b2- (tropical:) A ",[1,"cowardly"]," man; as also ↓ ",[2,"مِجْوَفٌ"],", and ↓ ",[2,"مُجَوَّفٌ"],"; the last explained in the K as meaning ",[1,"having no heart:"]," pl. [of the first] ",[2,"جُوفٌ"],". (TA.) ― -b3- A horse ",[1,"white in the"],[2,"جَوْف"]," [or ",[1,"belly"],"] ",[1,"as far as the part where the sides terminate,"]," whatever be the colour of the rest of him; (AO, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"مِجْوَفٌ"],". (TA.) [See also ",[2,"مُجَوَّفٌ"],".] ― -b4- In the conventional language of the science of inflection, (assumed tropical:) [A ",[1,"hollow"]," word; i. e.] a word ",[1,"having an infirm letter for its medial radical;"]," (K, TA;) as ",[2,"قَالَ"]," and ",[2,"بَاعَ"],". (TA.)"]},{"h":"مُجَافٌ","t":["(tropical:) A ",[1,"shut,"]," or ",[1,"closed,"]," door. (TA.)"]},{"h":"مَجُوفٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],"."]},{"h":"مِجْوَفٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"مُجَوَّفٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],", in three places. ― -b2- Also A beast ",[1,"whose"],[2,"بَلَق"]," [q. v.] ",[1,"reaches up to his belly:"]," (As, S, K:) or a horse ",[1,"whose"],[2,"بَلَق"],[1,"reaches to his sides"]," is said to be ",[2,"مُجَوَّفٌ بَلَقًا"],". (AA, TA.) [See also ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],", last meaning but one.] ― -b3- And an epithet applied to the bird called ",[2,"صُرَد"],", because it is ",[1,"white in the belly."]," (Mgh and Msb in art. ",[2,"صرد"],".)"]},{"h":"مُسْتَجَافٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"أَجْوَفُ"],"."]}]},"maqayis":["الجيم والواو والفاء كلمة واحدة، وهي جوف الشيء. يقال هذا جوف الإنسان، وجوف كل شيء. وطعنة جائفة، إذا وصلت إلى الجوف. وقدر جوفاء: واسعة الجوف. وجوف عير: مكان حماه رجل اسمه حمار. وفي المثل: \" أخلى من جوف عير \". وأصله رجل كان يحمي واديا له. وقد ذكر حديثه في كتاب العين."]}